* Creating a slice with make

Slices can be created with the built-in ⟪GTI18N_d057e6bf_000001⟫make⟪GTI18N_d057e6bf_000002⟫ function;
this is how you create dynamically-sized arrays.

The ⟪GTI18N_d057e6bf_000003⟫make⟪GTI18N_d057e6bf_000004⟫ function allocates a zeroed array
and returns a slice that refers to that array:

⟪GTI18N_d057e6bf_000005⟫

To specify a capacity, pass a third argument to ⟪GTI18N_d057e6bf_000006⟫make⟪GTI18N_d057e6bf_000007⟫:

⟪GTI18N_d057e6bf_000008⟫

⟪GTI18N_d057e6bf_000009⟫
